The projects that will be funded by the appropriation
contained in Republic Act No, 6960 must contribute to any or all of the
following objectives:
Preservation of life;
Restoration of home; and,
Resumption of production.
The following agencies shall be responsible for the identification of the
projects within their respective jurisdiction and whenever necessary, in
consultation with local government units, viz.:
Department of Public Works and Highways - for Roads,
Highways and Bridges, Flood Control and Seawalls, Water
Supply (level I), and Other Public Buildings and Facilities;
Philippine National Railways - for Railways;
Philippine Ports Authority - for Ports;
Air Transportation Office/Department of Transportation and
Communications - for Airports;
Postal Services Office/Department of Transportation and
Communications - for Post Offices;
Telecommunications Office/Department of Transportation
and Communications - for Telecommunication Facilities;
National Power Corporation - for Power Facilities;
National Electrification Administration - for Electrification
Facilities;
National Irrigation Administration - for Irrigation Facilities;

- 3 -
Department of Education, Culture and Sports - for
Schoolbuildings;
Department of Health - for Hospitals/Health Centers and
Public Health Programs;
National Housing Authority - for Housing Facilities;
Departier - National Defense - for Defense Facilities;
Export Processing Zone Authority - for Export Processing
Zone Facilities;
0)
Department of Social Welfare and Development - for Social
Welfare Projects;
Local Water and Utilities Administration - for Water Supply
Facilities (Levels Il and III); and,
Departments of Agriculture, Agrarian Reform, Environment
and Natural Resources, Labor and Employment and Trade
and Industry, Education, Culture and Sports, Local
Government, Tourism, and the National Livelihood Support
Fund - for Livelihood and Emergency Employment
Assistance Projects.
The above enumerated agencies shall also be responsible for the
implementation of the projects except those projects determined by the
Presidential Task Force to be more appropriately implemented by local
government units.
